 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nStruct star expansion not working properly\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using struct star expansion (e.g., `SELECT tbl.col.*` where `col` is a struct), the expansion is not happening correctly. The query should expand the struct fields but instead returns an empty result.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import optimizer\nfrom sqlglot.schema import MappingSchema\n\n# This should expand struct fields but doesn't work\nsql = \"WITH tbl1 AS (SELECT STRUCT(1 AS `f0`, 2 as f1) AS col) SELECT tbl1.col.* from tbl1\"\nschema = MappingSchema(schema=None, dialect='bigquery')\n\nresult = optimizer.qualify_columns.qualify_columns(\n    sqlglot.parse_one(sql, dialect='bigquery'), \n    schema=schema, \n    infer_schema=False\n)\n\nprint(\"Result:\", result.sql(dialect='bigquery'))\n# Expected: WITH tbl1 AS (SELECT STRUCT(1 AS `f0`, 2 AS f1) AS col) SELECT tbl1.col.`f0` AS `f0`, tbl1.col.f1 AS f1 FROM tbl1\n# Actual: WITH tbl1 AS (SELECT STRUCT(1 AS `f0`, 2 AS f1) AS col) SELECT FROM tbl1\n```\n\nThe struct star expansion should generate individual column selections for each field in the struct, but instead it's producing an empty SELECT list.\n</issue>\n",
